{"id":"fr.lc0001","meaning":"‹e› with an acute accent","note":"Always ay: ‹été› (ay-tay), summer."}
{"id":"fr.lc0002","meaning":"‹e› with a grave accent","note":"Always eh: ‹mère› (mehr), mother."}
{"id":"fr.lc0003","meaning":"‹e› with a circumflex","note":"Said eh, like ‹è›: ‹forêt› (foh-reh), forest."}
{"id":"fr.lc0004","meaning":"‹e› with two dots","note":"Say this ‹e› on its own, apart from the vowel before it: ‹Noël› (noh-ehl), Christmas."}
{"id":"fr.lc0005","meaning":"‹a› with a grave accent","note":"Same sound as ‹a›; it tells words apart: ‹à› (ah), to, at; ‹a› (ah), has."}
{"id":"fr.lc0006","meaning":"‹a› with a circumflex","note":"Said ah: ‹gâteau› (gah-toh), cake."}
{"id":"fr.lc0007","meaning":"‹i› with a circumflex","note":"Said ee: ‹île› (eel), island."}
{"id":"fr.lc0008","meaning":"‹i› with two dots","note":"Say this ‹i› on its own, apart from the vowel before it: ‹naïf› (nah-eef), naive."}
{"id":"fr.lc0009","meaning":"‹o› with a circumflex","note":"Said oh: ‹tôt› (toh), early."}
{"id":"fr.lc0010","meaning":"‹u› with a circumflex","note":"Said ew, like ‹u›: ‹sûr› (sewr), sure."}
{"id":"fr.lc0011","meaning":"‹u› with a grave accent","note":"Only in ‹où› (oo), where. ‹ou› without the accent means or."}
{"id":"fr.lc0012","meaning":"‹o› and ‹e› joined","note":"Usually in ‹œu›, said uh: ‹cœur› (kuhr), heart."}
{"id":"fr.lc0013","meaning":"oo, as in food","note":"‹nous› (noo), we"}
{"id":"fr.lc0014","meaning":"ee said with rounded lips","note":"‹tu› (tew), you"}
{"id":"fr.lc0015","meaning":"uh said with rounded lips","note":"‹bleu› (bluh), blue"}
{"id":"fr.lc0016","meaning":"a pure oh, no w at the end","note":"‹aussi› (oh-see), also"}
{"id":"fr.lc0017","meaning":"the same oh, three letters","note":"‹beau› (boh), beautiful"}
{"id":"fr.lc0018","meaning":"wah, as in the start of wander","note":"‹moi› (mwah), me"}
{"id":"fr.lc0019","meaning":"eh, as in bed","note":"‹lait› (leh), milk. The ‹t› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0020","meaning":"eh, the same sound as ‹ai›","note":"‹neige› (nehzh), snow"}
{"id":"fr.lc0021","meaning":"nasal ah, the ‹n› not said","note":"‹dans› (dahN), in"}
{"id":"fr.lc0022","meaning":"the same sound as ‹an›","note":"‹temps› (tahN), time; weather. The ‹p› and ‹s› are silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0023","meaning":"nasal oh","note":"‹bon› (bohN), good"}
{"id":"fr.lc0024","meaning":"nasal a, as in bag","note":"‹jardin› (zhahr-daN), garden"}
{"id":"fr.lc0025","meaning":"the same sound as ‹in›","note":"‹main› (maN), hand"}
{"id":"fr.lc0026","meaning":"nasal uh","note":"‹un› (uhN), one; a"}
{"id":"fr.lc0027","meaning":"hello; good morning","note":"‹on› is nasal ohN, ‹j› is zh, ‹ou› is oo. The final ‹r› is said."}
{"id":"fr.lc0028","meaning":"thank you","note":"‹c› before ‹i› is s."}
{"id":"fr.lc0029","meaning":"a lot, very much","note":"‹eau› is oh, ‹ou› is oo. The final ‹p› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0030","meaning":"three","note":"‹oi› is wah. The final ‹s› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0031","meaning":"house","note":"‹ai› is eh; one ‹s› between two vowels is z; ‹on› is nasal."}
{"id":"fr.lc0032","meaning":"bread","note":"‹ain› is nasal aN: no n sound."}
{"id":"fr.lc0033","meaning":"Monday","note":"‹un› is nasal uhN, then ‹di›."}
{"id":"fr.lc0034","meaning":"girl; daughter","note":"‹ill› is y. The final ‹e› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0035","meaning":"mountain","note":"‹on› is nasal, ‹gn› is ny. The final ‹e› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0036","meaning":"castle","note":"‹ch› is sh, ‹â› is ah, ‹eau› is oh."}
{"id":"fr.lc0037","meaning":"boy","note":"‹ç› is s, even before ‹o›; ‹on› is nasal."}
{"id":"fr.lc0038","meaning":"French (the language)","note":"‹an› is nasal, ‹ç› is s, ‹ai› is eh. The final ‹s› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0039","meaning":"hotel","note":"‹h› is silent, ‹ô› is oh. The final ‹l› is said (careful)."}
{"id":"fr.lc0040","meaning":"cheese","note":"‹g› before ‹e› is zh. The final ‹e› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0041","meaning":"two","note":"‹eu› is uh. The final ‹x› is silent."}
{"id":"fr.lc0042","meaning":"sister","note":"‹œu› is uh. The final ‹r› is said."}
{"id":"fr.lc0043","meaning":"four","note":"‹qu› is k. The final ‹e› is silent, so one syllable."}
{"id":"fr.lc0044","meaning":"the children","note":"Liaison: the silent ‹s› of ‹les› is said z before a vowel. ‹en› and ‹an› are both ahN; the ‹t› and ‹s› of ‹enfants› are silent."}
